W AX3051 1485-restrict-may-edges.ax:79:6-16 restriction-unverifiable "`fieldDirty` claims `restrict(no-foreign)` and the claim cannot be checked: the body may reach the `extern` item `danger` through a call through a field or a local that holds one of several functions: fieldDirty -> runHook -> viaDanger -> danger" ^51:6-13:"runHook" ^47:6-15:"viaDanger" ^-:"danger" ?"a limit of the ANALYSIS rather than a defect in the program - AX3037's argument at one remove. There are four readings: an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller and cannot be settled here at all, and - for `no-escape` alone - a region fixpoint that hit its round limit before the facts settled, which is a depth limit rather than anything about this declaration. Name the function at the call, stop calling the parameter, shorten the chain, or drop the claim; `no-cast`, `no-wrap` and `no-trap` are checked regardless, because all three are lexical and need no call resolved"
